      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "value": "I think this is a great idea. As a social interactive game it makes things difficult if only friends can join. If I make a friends only world and someone elses friend wants to join... the only ways to access my instance is by using 3rd party software to ask who the world owner is and send me a friendrequest. The other option would be inviting your friend out of the friends only world to ask who the worldowner is and send a friendsrequest. This is alot of trouble... therefore I think even friends only worlds can even get inviterights to the worldowner as a standard function. And the worldowner can still manage who comes in and who doesnt. I do not think we should have to rely on other software to see friends.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
