      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5b17f5f1fac4ad702bbde311",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "In my opinion this is just very confusing and kind of unnecessary. VRChat already has a huge learning curve for new players, (private vs public avatars, where to get avatars, how to upload an avatar, cloning, instance types, blocking, muting, safety, the culture, etc.) and this really only makes it worse. I found this difficult to read and understand and the name \"friends only+\" is so confusing. Maybe I'm just dumb who knows.\nI also have a hard time seeing where this is actually useful. From what I can see the largest convenience this has is if a friend forgets to go into orange, but you could just as easily making an invite+ world and set your status to blue. Friends of you could easily join by requesting off you, then friends of friends would have to request and get an invite back.\nAdding all that up, I don't think it's really worth the devs' time to implement this especially considering adding this to the game would be a fairly large undertaking both for the client and also the API. It's just really not worth it to me.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
