        "like": 4
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Hmm... at that point it would make more sense to just toss instance types as we know it, and make a Unix type permission system.\nThe first section would define if the Owner's friends need an invite, the second section would define the same for the Owner's friends, and the third would define it for everyone else.\nIt would be powerful, but potentially confusing.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
